03-02T16:32:01-08:00","id":1057327,"title":"","content":"Princess the Hopeful<br /> <br /> It's like exalted with charms, but set in a much more grim Cod world setting. It's interesting and one of the more 'complete' fan games, but in desperate need of editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T16:51:57-08:00","id":1057336,"title":"","content":"While it may cause screaming fits, how would you do 'magic girl' in cWoD? I guess you could use Sorcerer, but that would be rather low key. Perhaps you could add a power trait?<br /> <br /> Let us explore that for a bit. We will call the power trait Elpis (Greek for Hope). Elpis would be added as a dice pool modifier to Sorcerer rolls and would offer a pool. Points of Elpis could be spent to reduce time category (days to hours, hours to minutes, minutes to turns, or turns to instant), to stage down the type of damage from an attack (aggravated to lethal or lethal to bashing), or to stage up damage from an attack (bashing to lethal or lethal to aggravated). Characters would regain one point of Elpis per hour of rest (two per hour of meditation) or whenever they regain points of Willpower by fulfilling their Nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","